    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Studio Albums 93–16 is a 2018 box set by Suede on Demon Records that gathers the band’s studio albums from their 1993 debut through Night Thoughts (2016). Issued as a 10-LP set, it includes Suede, Dog Man Star, Coming Up, Head Music, A New Morning, Bloodsports, and Night Thoughts, presented across coloured vinyl discs and packaged as a numbered collector’s edition.\n\nThe set offers a compact overview of Suede’s evolution from their early Britpop/glam-rock peak into their later, more expansive and reflective work. The debut Suede introduced the band’s sleek, theatrical blend of rock and pop, while later albums trace shifts toward grander arrangements, sharper pop hooks, and a more mature, widescreen sound—making the collection especially appealing to listeners who want the group’s core studio catalog in one place.\n\nAs a curated anthology of the band’s principal albums rather than a hits package, Studio Albums 93–16 is significant for showing how Suede maintained a distinct identity across changing eras and lineups. Its focus on the original studio records, mastered from the original tapes, also makes it a notable archival release for fans and vinyl collectors.",
